import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'living':('A living giant the spell really hurts','A Necromancer considers Dispel Life against a hill giant five grids away. The game\'s drain hits living monsters: a native cast removes 66 HP. The original rating keeps damage only for monsters flagged both nonliving and undead — no monster in the game data has the nonliving flag — so the spell is valued below doing nothing. The correction rates it like the game: the launch value minus the mana cost of the spell.'),
 'undead':('Control: an undead bat the spell cannot hurt','A vampire bat is explicitly undead, and the game\'s drain leaves it untouched (native cast removes nothing). Both versions refuse the cast; only the raw number of the refusal differs. The corrected rating applies the chooser\'s standing mana penalty to a zero-damage launch instead of a dead filter.'),
 'bolt':('Control: the primary bolt is untouched','Only the class\'s primary nether bolt is valued against the same living giant. The Dispel Life filter plays no part, and the complete log is byte-identical before and after the correction.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/dispel-248 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw}
  for tag,key in (('RATING ','rating'),('OUTCOME ','outcome'),('LAUNCH ','launch')):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[key]={k:int(v) for k,v in re.findall(r'(\w+)=(-?\d+)',match[1])} if match else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Dispel Life was rated against nobody</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdbb;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native Dispel Life ratings and casts</p><h1>The Borg rated Dispel Life against nobody</h1><p>The game\'s Dispel Life hits every living monster in line of sight. The Borg\'s rating kept damage only for monsters flagged both nonliving and undead — the exact inverse — and since no monster in the game data carries the nonliving flag, the spell was valued below doing nothing against every enemy. Against this hill giant a native cast removes 66 HP.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">The rating</button><button data-step="1">The native cast</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p><p class="action"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the controls establish</h2><p>An undead vampire bat is immune in the game and both versions refuse the cast; the native cast removes nothing. The primary nether bolt\'s complete log is byte-identical before and after the correction: only the Dispel Life filter changed.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Necromancer level 26, depth 30, seed 1000, lit constructed arena, the Fear and Torment shadow book, Dispel Life and Nether Bolt learned, full mana, a torch. The production rating call and its damage expression are used unchanged; the native cast goes through the game\'s own command and its damage is measured on the monster\'s hit points. This isolates the rating filter, not full autonomous play; damage rolls are random, the rating is the average expression. No death or survival claim.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/248">issue248</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;let step=0;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=step===0?`Spell rating: ${d.rating?d.rating.value:'n/a'}`:(d.outcome?`Native cast removed ${d.outcome.hp_lost} HP`:'No cast in this control');p.querySelector('.state').textContent=step===0?(d.rating?`Average damage expression: ${d.rating.expected_average}.`:"The primary bolt rating, untouched by the filter."):'The native cast and its measured effect.';p.querySelector('.action').textContent=step===0?(d.passed&&d.rating&&d.rating.value>0?'A spell worth casting.':d.rating&&d.rating.value<0?'Valued below doing nothing — never cast.':''):(d.outcome&&d.outcome.hp_lost>0?'The drain really hurts the living giant.':d.outcome?'The undead bat is immune.':'');document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='living'?'The original values the spell at -21 while the game removes 66 HP; the correction values it at 19, the launch value minus the mana cost of the spell.':select.value==='undead'?'Both versions refuse the cast; the game leaves the undead bat untouched.':'The primary bolt log is byte-identical before and after.';for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.classList.toggle('active',Number(b.dataset.step)===step)}select.addEventListener('change',()=>{step=0;draw()});for(const b of document.querySelectorAll('[data-step]'))b.addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Number(b.dataset.step);draw()});draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
